.TH ASIS 1 "2026-10-27" "ASIS @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asis \- compose bounded searches for action plans against a knowledge base
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asis solve
.I task
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B asis run
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B asis kb
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B asis dashboard
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ASIS is an offline, deterministic constraint planner. A team of specialists
proposes action multisets, predicts their metrics and independently checks
the declared constraints. Residual-guided composition can retain intermediate
tradeoffs and search for compensating actions within explicit work limits.
The predictions describe the knowledge-base model, not observed measurements.
.PP
Solved results establish model feasibility. A bounded search does not establish
global optimality or infeasibility. Unsolved results mean no feasible plan was
found within the available search.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B solve
Solve the supplied task expression and print a report, or JSON with
.BR --json .
Exit 0 means solved, 2 means not solved, 3 means rejected before planning,
and 1 means an input or I/O error.
.TP
.B run
Solve the bundled demonstration task. A bare
.B asis
is shorthand for this command. Use
.B --no-trace
to avoid writing the default asis_trace.json file.
.TP
.B kb
List the active knowledge base's metrics, goals and actions. Use
.B --json
for a machine-readable representation.
.TP
.B dashboard
Serve a local browser dashboard backed by the planner. The default bind
address is 127.0.0.1 and the default port is 8765. Use
.B --port 0
to select an unused port,
.B --no-browser
to suppress opening a browser, or
.B --no-demo
to start without a demonstration task.
The desktop launcher opens a terminal with the dashboard server; press Ctrl+C
in that terminal to stop it. Closing the browser alone does not stop the server.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --kb " PATH_OR_NAME"
Use a JSON knowledge base or a bundled domain name such as web_service or
compensation. The default is web_service.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version.
.TP
.B --help
Print help for the command.
.SH SEARCH OPTIONS
The solve and run commands accept these options:
.TP
.BI --search-depth " N"
Maximum number of extension decisions in a composed repair (default 3).
Each decision also includes its required prerequisite actions.
.TP
.BI --beam-width " N"
Maximum number of deferred candidates retained per search layer (default 8).
.TP
.BI --search-evaluations " N"
Per-task model-evaluation allowance for composition (default 256).
Ordinary greedy repairs and optimizer evaluations are counted separately and
do not consume this composition allowance.
.TP
.BI --max-steps " N"
Maximum signal-delivery rounds (default 1000).
.PP
The solve command additionally accepts:
.TP
.BI --budget " N"
Message-delivery energy allowance (default 400). Model evaluations are
reported separately from message-delivery energy.
.TP
.BI --trace " PATH"
Write the full deterministic execution trace.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
asis solve 'latency <= 50ms * cost <= 100' --kb compensation --json
asis solve 'optimize_system' --budget 800 --trace run.json
asis dashboard --port 0
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/asis-swarm/asis
Private Python application and bundled knowledge-base domains.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/asis-swarm
README, license and release notes.
.SH SECURITY
The dashboard has no authentication and binds to localhost by default.
Use an appropriate trusted interface when changing the bind address.
.SH AUTHORS
ASIS contributors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR python3 (1)
